eric um  how long did it take uh between the  celebration the other night from  advancing to the finals  and everybody kind of digging back in to  what you guys need to do now going  forward  we did take a night just to acknowledge  it  and enjoy it  you know the players and the staff and  families that were here  i really do want i wanted everybody you  know to have perspective on  how difficult this is how extraordinary  of a  experience all of this is being part of  this bubble of being here for  80 plus days surviving all of it and  earning the right to compete for  an nba title um but we just got off a  very competitive hard fought  series and you know emotionally i don't  think anybody is ready just to  turn that page but yesterday was a work  day for the players it was a day just to  recover and relax and  we got together last night and did some  more prep today  next question tom deangelo hey eric  hey tom hey uh eric how is lebron  different today than he was the last  time he wore a heat uniform  uh you know i don't know but i i just  think it  is a true testament uh to his greatness  uh to be able to sustain this type of  success uh year in year out  different uh uniforms  uh and everybody you know new new  players and new teams  you know going after them uh  uh it's it's a real testament uh to that  commitment  um you know he's he's seen everything  you know at this point uh in his career  uh it's  it's just about winning and  his ability to do what he does  at his age is  is incredibly uncommon um but there's  there's a lot of work that goes behind  the scenes um  you know to be able to maintain that  next question kyle tucker from the  athletic  go ahead kyle i'm sorry about that uh  i know you've this has been talked about  before but uh  you guys you got a couple kentucky guys  there uh  one one's a boss and two have been a  huge part of this run  and you've i know you've sort of  addressed it but  what is it about kentucky guys do you  think they're the two you have anyway  and about their kentucky experience do  you think that has prepared them  to be ready for such a stage so soon  well we have to have a few kentucky guys  on our team  because my boss that's like a  prerequisite  uh somehow someway we got to get  somebody uh from  his alma mater on on our roster uh  this seems this final seems like a  great recruiting pitch for cal doesn't  it and i'm  i'm not sure he's going to maximize that  we we love kentucky players because  you're there  to get better to be pushed uh to  understand  uh what it means uh to play for our team  play  play a role uh and to train  uh to become a pro at this level you're  going to face good competition in  practice  you're going to be expected to work and  it's a it's an environment that as much  as it  possibly can prepare you  for the pros even though it's at the  collegiate level  you know our two guys played  significantly different roles  for kentucky when they're in college and  that was part of the thing that we liked  they're both willing to play a role  young players often times it's just  about  how many shots they can get how many  touches scores  so they can improve their draft process  but if you just watch all of those  games of tyler and bam  you know when we when we met with them  they both said hey we're  capable of doing more but you always  take that with a grain of salt every  player says that  but they truly did just commit to to a  role and  worked like crazy behind the scenes uh  on their player development  and it's been obviously just a  a good fit with us their mentality and  how we are  in person tim reynolds on your right  spo so much got made and much still gets  made about how lebron changed after  2011.  how much did going through that change  you  as well i mean it seemed like that's  when there was like a further commitment  to position lists and  putting together guys as groups instead  of just individuals and figuring how you  can play guys  as five instead of where one guy would  fit it just seemed like a lot of change  with you that off season too  how much did going through that help you  out as well  those are great professional and life  experiences  to be able to have that opportunity to  grow and  you know the first two teams i coached  as a head coach were  much different than that whole  experience and the game started to  change  you know during that run and we had to  adapt and adjust  accordingly but you know i learned and  grew  in the nba in the 90s  under pat and then the early 2000s you  look at those  games systematically and schematically  and just  stylistically to compare where it is  right now it's  two different sports so i'm just very  grateful that i had that opportunity to  be able to  to grow and  be on that journey with that group that  was  an amazing team and everything that came  about it  um in many ways just my personality  i hated it and  you know i'm an introvert so i don't  like you know that but i think it was  good to go through that sometimes you  know even as a professional just to get  out of your comfort zone and  embrace it and and see what happens when  you get out on the other side of it  it was it feels like a totally different  chapter in my life but i'm  truly grateful to be around uh those  special players that  group that was so committed uh to coming  together to compete for titles  dave here on the front eric how long did  it take you to come to terms  um back in 2014 after lebron left to  recognize  you know that there's going to be  another chapter and then what's been  like to see him  make five more finals appearances since  you guys part at least  uh yeah the the  first part of that uh you know we went  through the whole process i went through  my own  you know six week uh reflection period  uh that summer um but then you get back  to work that's  we've we've built a lot of different  teams over the years and  and we've been conditioned  to to move on and give everything your  heart and soul to the next  group and the next team and we really  thought that we had  a championship contending team that next  year  that's how we approached it  however doesn't it's irrelevant what  anybody else thought we knew  that we were losing um but when we made  that mid-season trade for gorham we made  a problem promise to him that we would  be competing for titles  it was just so unfortunate uh that cb  wasn't able to finish the season but we  owed it to goran to fight for it and go  for it and we ended up  fighting for the playoffs dwayne missed  25 games but we were just there at the  end  we got knocked out of the playoffs with  um three days to go  but you gained that experience i think  it was important to show gorn that we  are not going to tank and we're going to  continue to build and  the next year was uh the year that we  were able to go to game seven we thought  that was a  legit contending team and we had that  just really really tough seven game  series with toronto weren't able to make  it to the conference finals  to play against cleveland we thought  we really had a chance uh that year  um and that's what this game does to you  sometimes it breaks your heart  uh that that you really broke our heart  we thought we  we really had a good run in us  um and that was the second year that's  where  cb again had had to step away  uh but then to see you know what  lebron has done when he moved on to  cleveland and to hear  it really is just a testament to uh  his greatness and his commitment to  winning  and to be able to do it uh with  different rosters  and uniforms is is really remarkable  thank you coach goran will be right up  thank you

